EVERY REMOVED FLOW IS ATTRIBUTED TO A REMOVED ROW BY NAME, read off the old
arm's own evidence rather than inferred from totals: simplex-chat 13/13 are STM
cells (readTVarIO x7, atomically x3, readTVar, newTVar, newTVarIO); git 5/5 are
socket. ejabberd is the load-bearing case -- 2 false sources removed, 3 GENUINE
ETS reads KEPT (lookup_element, tab2list, table_info), so the claim stays
violated on real evidence instead of being blanket-cleared.

net_send moved -4 and I had listed it as a control; that classification was
mine and it was wrong. gen_udp.open was declared under BOTH net_send and
net_recv and both were removed, so net_send is a TOUCHED boundary. The -4 is
exactly the two erlang/elixir repos.

TESTS. A new file pins all three families, the two costly controls, and the
mechanism itself (a test asserting db_read/net_recv really are auto-source
boundaries, so the rationale cannot quietly stop applying). Three io_boundary
tests were RE-VEHICLED, not weakened -- they used removed rows as fixtures for
mechanisms unrelated to this change (cgo resolution, ambiguous-name matching,
multi-include module slots); each keeps its assertion and gains a row that
still ships. sendto rather than send for the cgo case, because `send` is in c's
ambiguous_names and the gate correctly refuses a bare name.

test_multi_boundary_ruling's live-corpus test required all four reasons to
occur, which fails the moment the last declared debt is paid -- a test that
punishes success. It now asserts the three SETTLED reasons plus agreement
between the live unruled count and the register, and the resolver's `unruled`
branch is exercised on a synthetic catalogue, which is where that invariant
belongs: the branch must WORK, not the debt must EXIST.

LIMITS. violated -> inconclusive is not a safety result. F3's JAVA arm is
UNMEASURED -- playframework moved no db_read, so the JPA removal rests on the
argument, not evidence; F3's elixir arm did move (plausible db_read 55 -> 48).
One cohort's measurement is not a precision figure and does not update 0006.

